PenguinBox — licensing
======================

PenguinBox is a fork of xemu, which is a fork of QEMU. The distribution
includes both the emulator and various firmware files. These are separate
programs distributed together for convenience, and they have separate
licenses.

1) The emulator as a whole is released under the GNU General Public License,
   version 2 (GPLv2). A copy is in COPYING.

2) Parts of the emulator carry specific licenses compatible with GPLv2, so
   each source file contains its own licensing information. Source files with
   no licensing information are released under the GNU General Public License,
   version 2 or (at your option) any later version.

3) Code written specifically for this fork — the VR support and the Steel
   Battalion device, overlay and performance work — is licensed MIT, which
   flows cleanly into the GPLv2 aggregate and remains reusable on its own.
   Those files carry an explicit SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT header.

   One exception, stated because it is not ours to relicense:
   hw/xbox/xid-steel-battalion.c derives from xemu's hw/xbox/xid.c and carries
   the copyrights of its original authors. It remains LGPL-2.0-or-later.

4) The firmware files in pc-bios/ and the ROM submodules referenced by
   .gitmodules are separate works under their own licenses; see the
   corresponding upstream projects. Submodules are not vendored into this
   archive — .gitmodules records the pinned revisions so they can be fetched.

5) No Xbox BIOS, MCPX boot ROM, EEPROM, or game media is included in or
   distributed with this software.

The overwhelming majority of this software is the work of the QEMU and xemu
projects and their contributors. See MAINTAINERS and the per-file copyright
headers.
